.TH MYSTRCPY 3 "September 2026" "libmyutils 1.0" "libmyutils Manual"
.SH NAME
mystrcpy \- copy a string
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include "mystrfunctions.h"
.sp
.BI "int mystrcpy(char *" dest ", const char *" src ");"
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B mystrcpy()
copies the string pointed to by
.I src,
including the terminating null byte, into the buffer pointed to by
.IR dest .
The caller is responsible for ensuring that
.I dest
is large enough to hold the copied string.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns 0 on success, and \-1 on failure.
